es/130120"} "Marie-Florence Candassamy"] " (2)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Sun was upset early, losing her first match to the #30 seed from Japan, " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101998"} "Miho Yoshimura"] ". Candassamy also faltered, losing her second match to Sun’s teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/151888"} "Yu Sihan"] ", who was seeded 18th."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Kong had no such trouble, moving to the final easily, where she faced France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/130114"} "Auriane Mallo-Breton"] ", who had been the silver medalist earlier in the year at the European Championships. Mallo-Breton took a 4-0 lead in the first period, but Kong chiseled away at it and eventually prevailed, 13-12, to take the gold medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Kong’s gold was only the second fencing medal ever for Hong Kong, China, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/134324"} "Edgar Cheung"] "’s gold in the 2020 men’s individual foil, although Cheung would repeat as gold medalist two days later in Paris."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The bronze medal match between Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/151924"} "Eszter Muhari"] " and Estonia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/151911"} "Nelli Differt"] " went to overtime, with Muhari taking the medal, 15-14."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Seed"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/130486"} "Vivian Kong"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HKG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HKG.png"}] "HKG"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "6"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/130114"} "Auriane Mallo-Breton"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.